Package: coiCheckR
Title: Screen Peer Reviewer Candidates for Conflicts of Interest
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Janani", "Ravi", email = "janani.ravi@cuanschutz.edu",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Screens candidate peer reviewers (for journal manuscripts or
    grant applications) against a manuscript's author list for conflicts
    of interest. Builds co-authorship evidence from PubMed/PMC via
    'rentrez', resolves NIH-funded shared-award conflicts via the NIH
    RePORTER API, and enriches preprint records via the bioRxiv API.
    Detects direct co-authorship, time-windowed co-authorship (e.g. the
    NIH "last 4 years" rule), second-degree co-authorship (a candidate's
    frequent collaborators overlapping with an author's), and shared
    federal funding. Returns a tidy, auditable conflict report rather
    than a silent accept/reject decision, since COI judgment calls
    should stay with the editor.
